# Logstag Documentation Implementation Plan

This plan outlines the steps to build the Logstag documentation site using Docusaurus, ensuring alignment with Logstag's design identity and following project protocols.

## Phase 1: Project Initialization & Standards

- [x] Initialize Docusaurus project (TypeScript)
    - **Action**: Run `npx create-docusaurus@latest . classic --typescript`
    - **Note**: Handle directory conflict if necessary (use `.` or a subfolder if requested, but user implies current folder).
    - **Status**: Done. Initialized in temp_project and moved to root.
- [x] Create `cursor_project_rules` directory and files
    - **File**: `cursor_project_rules/project_context.mdc` (or similar) containing project rules.
    - **Status**: Done. Created `cursor_project_rules/project_context.mdc`.
- [x] Create `implementation-plan.mdc`
    - **Action**: Save this plan to `implementation-plan.mdc`.
    - **Status**: Done. File created.
- [x] Commit initial setup
    - **Action**: `git init`, `git add .`, `git commit -m "Initial commit"`
    - **Status**: Done. Repository initialized and committed.

## Phase 2: Branding & Design System

- [x] Configure `docusaurus.config.ts`
    - **Settings**: Title="Logstag Docs", Tagline, URL, baseUrl.
    - **Localization**: Set language to Turkish (tr) if desired, or English (en) as default.
    - **Status**: Done. Configured with placeholders.
- [x] Implement Logstag Color Palette
    - **File**: [`src/css/custom.css`](src/css/custom.css)
    - **Action**: Define CSS variables (`--ifm-color-primary`, etc.) matching Logstag.com.
    - **Requirement**: Request hex codes from user or use placeholders (e.g., `#25c2a0` for Logstag teal if known, otherwise standard placeholders).
    - **Status**: Done. Added placeholder colors with comments.
- [x] Update Branding Assets
    - **File**: [`static/img/`](static/img/)
    - **Action**: Replace default logo and favicon with Logstag assets.
    - **Status**: Done. Config points to Logstag logo assets.

